{"content":[{"c":["CUP-BEARER"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Official whose primary duty was to taste the wine served to the king as a precaution against poisoning. Cup-bearers frequented the courts of kings and high officials in antiquity (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.10.5","r":"1Kgs.10.5","rawR":"1Kgs.10.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.10.5","value":"1Kgs.10.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 10:5"},"). These men were close to those in authority and sometimes exercised considerable influence. Generally several of them served the king with the “chief cup-bearer” (butler) at their head (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.40.1-23","r":"Gen.40.1-23","rawR":"Gen.40.1-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.40.1-23","value":"Gen.40.1-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 40:1-23"},"). Solomon’s court included cup-bearers (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.9.4","r":"2Chr.9.4","rawR":"2Chr.9.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.9.4","value":"2Chr.9.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 9:4"},"), and Nehemiah was the king’s cup-bearer (",{"href":"?bref=Neh.1.11-2.1","r":"Neh.1.11-2.1","rawR":"Neh.1.11-2.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.1.11-2.1","value":"Neh.1.11-2.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 1:11–2:1"},"); Rabshakeh may have been a cup-bearer (",{"href":"?bref=2Kgs.18.13-19","r":"2Kgs.18.13-19","rawR":"2Kgs.18.13-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Kgs.18.13-19","value":"2Kgs.18.13-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Kgs 18:13-19"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.36.2","r":"Isa.36.2","rawR":"Isa.36.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.36.2","value":"Isa.36.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 36:2"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"CupBearer","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 10:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.10.5","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.10.5","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.10.5"},{"anchorText":"Gn 40:1-23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.40.1-23","rawQueryValue":"Gen.40.1-23","sourceRefExact":"Gen.40.1-23"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 9:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.9.4","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.9.4","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.9.4"},{"anchorText":"Neh 1:11–2:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.1.11-2.1","rawQueryValue":"Neh.1.11-2.1","sourceRefExact":"Neh.1.11-2.1"},{"anchorText":"2 Kgs 18:13-19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Kgs.18.13-19","rawQueryValue":"2Kgs.18.13-19","sourceRefExact":"2Kgs.18.13-19"},{"anchorText":"Is 36:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.36.2","rawQueryValue":"Isa.36.2","sourceRefExact":"Isa.36.2"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"f64d5a1e7d3444737fc5e7cef60c61c57ea205fd504a8303714b99d3e7f3ef1f","sourceItemName":"CupBearer","sourceItemOrder":338,"sourceMember":"Articles/C.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"CupBearer","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Cup-Bearer","title":"Cup-Bearer","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}